+## Failed session startup
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, both buffered and streaming callers receive that same error after `onError(session, error)` and `afterSession(session)` run in that order (provided those hooks complete normally); both hooks receive the original session. `afterSession` is cleanup even after partial startup: `beforeSession` may have allocated resources before throwing, but user-input hooks and model processing have not run, and cleanup must tolerate resources that were never allocated ([validated by: reports and cleans up a failed beforeSession before rejecting the caller with the original error](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
